      "level": 1,
      "content": "Using Layout System in HTML"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Instead of styling each section separately, add .container class on each section for the same layout throughout."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "<header>\n  <div class=\"container\">\n    <h1>Learning HTML Blog</h1>\n  </div>\n</header>\n\n<main class=\"container\">\n  ...\n</main>\n\n<section class=\"form-wrapper\">\n  <div class=\"container\">\n    ...\n  </div>\n</section>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Lets also add a card layout system to our project."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "<main class=\"container\">\n  ...\n</main>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now:"
    },
    {
      "type": "numbered_list",
      "items": [
        "layout rules live in one place",
        "spacing feels consistent",
        "changes are easy and safe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This is CSS as a system, not stitched parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
